Roadmap & Q&A

Slide: Elevator pitch

A lightweight, client-side weather UI that shows current, hourly, 5-day and weekly forecasts, lets users save favourite locations, and includes an interactive map (Leaflet optional).
Designed for speed, progressive enhancement and easy offline testing.
Slide: Key features (user-facing)

Search by city (typeahead planned) and use-device location
Current weather card with:
Icon, temp, humidity, wind, “feels like”, and AQI
Save as favourite / Remove favourite
Forecast views: Hourly, 5‑day, Weekly (One Call)
Favorites modal (persisted in localStorage)
Responsive layout; About page with image + content; client-only contact form (testing only)
Slide: Implementation & tech stack

Frontend: plain HTML + Bootstrap 5 for layout and components
Styling: styles.css (variables for nav height & spacing)
App logic: app.js (main), js/5-day-forecast.js, js/weekly-forecast.js, save-locations.js
Optional map: Leaflet (loaded only where included)
Data: OpenWeatherMap APIs (current / forecast / air pollution)
Persistence: localStorage for favourites and contact submissions
Slide: High-level architecture

index.html — main UI, includes scripts in this order:
config.local.js (API key variable)
5-day and weekly forecast module scripts
save-locations.js
app.js (main glue)
app.js responsibilities:
Build and render weather card and forecast areas
Wire search controls, auto-refresh, and favorites interactions
Fetch helpers and UI update functions
save-locations.js: small module for localStorage favorites API (get/save/remove/clear)
Slide: Live demo script (3–5 mins)

Start local server (project root):
python -m http.server 8000
Open http://localhost:8000
Show search bar: enter “London” → Click Search
Show current weather card, map centering (if map enabled), hourly/daily/weekly toggles
Click “Save as favourite” → Open Favorites modal → show saved item
Remove favourite from modal
Demonstrate contact form on About page (submit → shows “Thank you!” and saved to localStorage)
Resize viewport to show responsive behavior
Slide: Manual test highlights (quick)

No API key: app warns and fails gracefully (no crashes)
With valid key: search returns weather, forecasts populate
Favorites persist across page reloads in localStorage
Contact form: stored locally; shows success message “Thank you!”
Map: only initializes where Leaflet included; app avoids crashing otherwise
Slide: Known issues & gotchas

Leaflet map requires the Leaflet CSS/JS to be present on the page — otherwise init will fail
Some modules expose globals for compatibility (save-locations uses a window shim)
Geocoding rate limits if using external APIs — add debounce/caching for production
AQI requires a valid OpenWeatherMap key and may require paid permissions for One Call in some plans
Slide: Security & privacy notes

No user data is sent to a backend (contact form is client-side only)
API keys are expected to be provided in config.local.js (not committed)
Favorites stored in the user’s browser (localStorage)
Slide: Roadmap / next steps

Add typeahead/autocomplete with debounce + caching
Convert to ES modules (import/export) for cleaner dependency management
Add unit/e2e smoke tests (Puppeteer / Playwright)
Improve favorites UI: sidebar, badges, counts
Add server-side proxy for caching API calls & hiding keys (optional)
Optimize map loading (lazy load Leaflet only when map visible)
Slide: Troubleshooting tips (for demo)

If map shows “L is not defined”, ensure Leaflet scripts are included in the page before app.js
If no forecast appears, check console for 401/403 — likely missing/invalid OPENWEATHER_API_KEY
Use DevTools → Application → Local Storage to inspect favourites/contactSubmissions
